
Ubuntu was installed on Windows using wsl --install, followed by username and password creation.
The Ubuntu environment was verified using uname -a and lsb_release -a.
GCC was configured and installed using sudo apt update and sudo apt install gcc.
A basic C program was created, compiled using GCC, and executed to verify the development environment.
A Git repository was initialized using git init to manage the practical files.
The shell environment and running processes were examined using echo $SHELL and ps.
The project structure was created to organize the source files and practical work.
Process abstraction was studied using fork(), which creates a child process from a parent process.
The exec() family was used to replace the current process with another executable program.
Parent and child process IDs were displayed to understand their relationship.
The process hierarchy was observed using the pstree command.
System calls were traced using strace ls to observe how a program interacts with the operating system.
These activities provided practical understanding of Linux processes, process creation, program execution, and system-level operations.
